course: dictionary
lesson: 12877
title: Formal words: ensue
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to serious writing, like reports, news and exam papers. «Ensue» is one of them. It means to happen after something, as a result of it.
explain: «The bell rang, and a loud cheer ensued.» The bell came first, and the cheer followed because of it. You could also say «then a loud cheer happened» or «that led to a loud cheer».
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in an easier word. «After the argument, a long silence ensued.» Try «followed»: «a long silence followed» still makes sense, so you have found the meaning.
fact: «Ensue» means to happen after something, and because of it.
fact: «Ensue» can also mean to come next in time.
fact: «Ensue» is a verb, so it changes: ensues, ensued, ensuing.
fact: Easy swaps for «ensue» are «followed», «resulted» and «came next».
fact: «Ensue» is formal, so you will meet it more in stories and exam papers than in everyday talk.
exercise: «The teacher dropped her pen, and a noisy scramble ensued.» What does ensued mean here? | Stopped suddenly | Was lost forever | Was painted red | *Happened after, as a result
exercise: «The power went out, and panic ensued.» Which word means the same as ensued? | danced | forgot | slept | *followed
exercise: Jayden says ensued means «the game ended». Is he right? | *No, it means happened after and because of something | Yes, it means it was over and finished | Yes, it means the game was over | No, it means ran away fast
test: «The alarm went off, and confusion ensued.» What does ensued mean here? | *Came after, as a result | Went missing | Was forgotten | Ended quickly
test: Which sentence uses ensue correctly? | The dog ensued the ball. | *Shouting ensued after the prize was announced. | Ensue is a colour of paint. | I ensued my lunch.
exam: Read: «The vase fell, and a crash ensued.» Choose the best meaning of ensued. | *Followed as a result | Broke into pieces | Was caught by someone | Was hidden under the table
